WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.019 --> 00:00:02.401
(audience cheering)
(uptempo music)

00:00:02.401 --> 00:00:04.411
- [Kelly] How are you?
- Nice to see you, I'm great.

00:00:04.411 --> 00:00:05.290
- [Kelly] I know, now we're in New York.

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:06.840
- We're in New York.
- The last time

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.580
we were in LA when you came, yeah, yeah.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:09.450
- [Theresa] Now you're on my turf.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:10.500
- I know, I like it.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:11.760
I love it here.
- Isn't it amazing?

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.242
There's nothing like New York.
- [Kelly] Yeah, you've been

00:00:13.242 --> 00:00:14.075
very busy here.
- [Theresa] Yes.

00:00:14.075 --> 00:00:16.110
- Yes, you have a new
podcast right now, right?

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:16.943
Do you love it?

00:00:16.943 --> 00:00:17.776
- I do, I love.

00:00:17.776 --> 00:00:18.990
It's called "Hey Spirit!"

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:21.240
And I love being able to connect people,

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.910
you know, all over the world
and, you know, over a Zoom.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:26.370
It's amazing on how
Spirit really validates

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:28.800
that they're still with us,
it's absolutely incredible.

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:31.110
- Yeah, and it's also
like even scheduling too

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:32.190
in your life, like it's kind of cool,

00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:34.380
you can schedule a
podcast more around you.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:35.848
Which is nice.
- Right?

00:00:35.848 --> 00:00:38.160
- Well, Theresa says she connects to those

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.650
who have passed on through
something she calls Spirit.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:42.570
So you say Spirit guides you,

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:45.120
but do you ever feel
that, like physically?

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.910
- Yeah, so what happens is
a lot of times when souls,

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:49.740
when they first start
to communicate with me,

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:51.420
they make me feel like the bond

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:53.340
that they shared with the person.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:54.173
But a lot of times

00:00:54.173 --> 00:00:55.680
they'll just bring me
through the departure,

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.660
they'll make me feel what they felt

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:59.610
as the soul left the physical body.

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:01.976
- That seems rude.
- Yeah, well, not rude.

00:01:01.976 --> 00:01:03.136
(both laughing)

00:01:03.136 --> 00:01:04.110
- Oh my God, it seems hard.
- It was rude-

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:05.220
it is very hard.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:07.170
I would say I make what
I do look very easy,

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:08.520
it's the hardest thing that I have to do,

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:10.200
is to stand in front of someone

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.800
and take them on this
emotional rollercoaster

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:15.450
of feeling pain, sorrow, loss, and grief.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:16.770
And then try to give them peace,

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:18.960
and a little bit of levity and laughter

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:21.030
to know that their loved
ones are still with us.

00:01:21.030 --> 00:01:23.130
And that's one of the
reasons why I do what I do,

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:26.220
it's not people to believe
in what I do, I don't care.

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:27.900
I want people to believe in themselves,

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:29.250
to believe in an afterlife,

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:31.410
to know that their loved one's souls

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:33.510
are still with them
just in a different way,

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:37.200
and just to embrace those
things that remind you of them.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.000
- That's beautiful.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.770
So whenever you, say you feel it,

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:43.080
like, do you actually feel it physically,

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.210
like feel affected?

00:01:45.210 --> 00:01:46.920
- Yeah, like I could feel like,

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:49.020
I already knew when I
was standing back there

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:52.320
that there was a real
tragedy of a departure

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.330
because I kept like tasting blood,

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:57.690
and I kept feeling like
a blow to my chest, so.

00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:58.743
- Like in the room, like in here-

00:01:58.743 --> 00:02:00.870
- When I was standing back
there getting ready to...

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:01.800
Yeah, back there.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:05.940
- Oh, that, wow, that's heavy.

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:08.370
'Cause then you don't wanna
walk out there and go, "Hey."

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:09.540
- Well, you know, that's the thing,

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:11.610
you know, people came here today,

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:13.890
they didn't come to
maybe expect to see me,

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:15.240
they came to see you, right?

00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:16.770
They didn't know I was coming.
- [Kelly] Yeah, yeah.

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:17.670
- And that's what I always say,

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:20.730
Spirit gives us exactly what we need

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:22.473
to kind of restore our faith,

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.410
and to know that they are okay,

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:28.470
and more importantly, that
their soul is at peace.

00:02:28.470 --> 00:02:31.170
- It provides probably so
much closure for people,

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:34.110
in just such a peaceful way.
- It does.

00:02:34.110 --> 00:02:36.720
You can't imagine how many people pass,

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:39.030
and what people are left
with for whatever reason.

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:40.350
- [Kelly] The (indistinct).

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:41.730
- And some people come, they
don't wanna live anymore,

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:43.440
they don't know how.

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:44.520
There are times where people

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.350
haven't spoken to other family members

00:02:46.350 --> 00:02:48.300
because someone died.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:49.890
And someone will come to a reading,

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:51.870
and it will restore their faith,

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:54.390
it'll give them a purpose to live,

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:56.640
they'll reunite families
that haven't spoken.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:58.800
- [Kelly] Powerful, yeah.
- So it's so much more

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:01.050
than just communicating
with people that have died.

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:02.940
- Absolutely, oh, so your new show,

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:05.670
it say combines readings and
your personal life, right?

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:06.503
- Correct.

00:03:06.503 --> 00:03:07.380
- So this is like full on,

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:09.090
do you mind being on
camera a lot like that,

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:09.923
like all the time?

00:03:09.923 --> 00:03:11.250
- It's so crazy, like I don't even realize

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:12.300
that they're there-
- [Kelly] I don't either,

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.190
I think that's not normal.
- [Theresa] It's normal.

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:15.243
But I don't either.

00:03:15.243 --> 00:03:16.076
- [Theresa] To me its normal.
- 'Cause they'll be like,

00:03:16.076 --> 00:03:16.909
"Do you mind the cameras here?"

00:03:16.909 --> 00:03:18.210
I'm like, "What cameras?"

00:03:18.210 --> 00:03:19.800
We'll be somewhere, and
I didn't even see it.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:21.000
- Well, I talked to dead people,

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.650
so they always around, and
nobody else could see it.

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:24.752
So to me at cameras-
(everyone laughing)

00:03:24.752 --> 00:03:26.190
- You're like, "They're always here."

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:28.527
- Yes, but it's the most
natural thing for me.

00:03:28.527 --> 00:03:30.510
And the thing that I love
about "Raising Spirits,"

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.430
it's 'cause I am on the road so much.

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:35.970
And I'm away a lot, and
so they're on, you know,

00:03:35.970 --> 00:03:38.130
on the bus with me, they're
seeing what it's like

00:03:38.130 --> 00:03:41.280
in a day of a life of me, and then-

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:42.600
- I think people will probably see

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:44.700
how draining it must be and feel,

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.070
and that's an emotional roller coaster

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:48.000
all the time, every time

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.100
you're talking with someone.
- It sure is, it sure is.

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:50.933
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:50.933 --> 00:03:51.810
- But I wouldn't trade what I do

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:53.040
for anything in the physical world.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:55.200
I consider it an honor and a privilege

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.910
to be able to share my gift,

00:03:56.910 --> 00:03:59.370
and to give someone
some peace and comfort.

00:03:59.370 --> 00:04:00.480
- [Kelly] Beautiful.
- And the fact that people

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:03.600
trust me with the souls of
their departed loved ones,

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:04.830
means the absolute world to me.

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:06.786
So it's an honor to do what I do.

00:04:06.786 --> 00:04:08.973
(audience applauding)
- So you told us before,

00:04:08.973 --> 00:04:10.830
but remind us what it's like for you

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:12.330
when you start connecting.

00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:14.940
- So what happens is I just
feel immediately drawn.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:16.110
So I was drawn to this area,

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:18.960
but I was more drawn
to this area over here,

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:20.793
down here, and up in here.

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:24.930
And I just keep feeling,
there's just one soul

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:28.440
that keeps bringing me through
a very traumatic departure.

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:31.440
So I keep getting like
a blow to the chest,

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:32.610
and I keep tasting blood,

00:04:32.610 --> 00:04:36.210
so that's my symbol for where
someone passed tragically.

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:39.210
And I always say, you
know, like I said earlier,

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.980
like nobody came here today thinking that

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:43.230
they might hear from their
loved one that has died.

00:04:43.230 --> 00:04:44.760
I always deliver messages-
- [Kelly] So that's heavy.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.520
- It is because sometimes
someone might be afraid,

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.720
or not know what to expect

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:52.020
when their loved one does come
through, what they might say.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:53.070
But I can guarantee you

00:04:53.070 --> 00:04:55.623
it will always be things
of faith and healing,

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:58.830
so I don't want anyone to be afraid.

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:01.503
Do you understand the
tragedy up over here, ma'am?

00:05:04.042 --> 00:05:06.720
- I mean, (indistinct) passed a week ago.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:07.743
- A week ago, okay.

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:10.830
And very tragic, is that correct?

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:12.370
Yeah.
- [Theresa] Okay.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:14.370
- What!
- Yeah, actually.

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:17.400
- So now do you feel like a chill,

00:05:17.400 --> 00:05:19.410
or like some type of
warmth move through you?

00:05:19.410 --> 00:05:20.243
- A warmth, yeah.

00:05:20.243 --> 00:05:22.200
- [Theresa] Okay, I asked
the soul to move through you

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:24.150
to validate that the soul is present.

00:05:24.150 --> 00:05:24.983
- Wow.

00:05:24.983 --> 00:05:26.310
- [Theresa] Because the
reason why this is happening

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:28.140
because you and the family are afraid

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:30.270
that the soul is not
safe in a peace with God,

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:31.800
is that correct?

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:33.820
- I mean, I think so, right?
- Yeah.

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:34.830
- Yeah, yeah.

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:35.910
- [Theresa] Is that correct?
- Yeah.

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:37.920
- So just know that this is the soul's way

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:40.590
of validating that they are okay,

00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:42.300
and more importantly,

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:45.510
that we could not have
prevented this departure.

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:46.800
- [Audience Member] Wow.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:48.960
- Do you understand that?
- Yeah, yeah.

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:49.793
- Because I felt like

00:05:49.793 --> 00:05:53.040
I needed to take responsibility
for my departure.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:54.347
- Wow!

00:05:54.347 --> 00:05:57.180
- Do you understands
the car accident, okay?

00:05:57.180 --> 00:05:59.370
Were you just talking to them?
- Yes!

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:00.900
- They're telling me that, I go,

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:02.700
you're messing up this
reading over here, I'm trying

00:06:02.700 --> 00:06:04.320
to do this reading here-
- I'm so sorry.

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:06.990
- So what I love about that-
- I'm so sorry, what?

00:06:06.990 --> 00:06:10.050
- Validating for you that they heard you,

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:11.880
do you understand that?
- Yes.

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:13.560
What plans changed that day?

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:14.850
'Cause what happened is
they put me in the car,

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:16.260
and they switched my seat.

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:18.210
So that's my symbol for
that, plans change that day,

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:21.003
they switched cars, or
they switched drivers.

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:23.940
- What?

00:06:23.940 --> 00:06:26.910
- Well, we were supposed
to go out together.

00:06:26.910 --> 00:06:30.000
I stayed home, I acted like I was asleep.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.880
And she wet with my best friend,

00:06:32.880 --> 00:06:34.620
it was both of them in the car.

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:37.800
And usually when we went out together,

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:40.680
I always took a ride with the best friend.

00:06:40.680 --> 00:06:43.350
But since I wasn't there, my sister did

00:06:43.350 --> 00:06:45.784
'cause she didn't like
going in the car with her.

00:06:45.784 --> 00:06:47.686
And they died, they both died-

00:06:47.686 --> 00:06:49.211
- [Theresa] And you have
been carrying this burden

00:06:49.211 --> 00:06:52.323
for years, for decades.
- Oh my god,

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:54.390
- Validating for you

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:56.760
that they do not want
you to carry this burden

00:06:56.760 --> 00:06:58.260
of feeling that if you were there,

00:06:58.260 --> 00:07:01.020
or somehow you could
have been responsible,

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:02.460
do you understand that?

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:05.100
Or if you went this
never would've happened.

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:07.437
- Yeah, tell her I missed
her and I love so much.

00:07:07.437 --> 00:07:09.750
- You just did, ma'am.
- Oh!

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:10.680
- She also just told me

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:12.360
that you connect with
the song on the radio

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:13.560
that reminds you of her-
- Always!

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:15.412
- It's not a current top 40 hit, right?

00:07:15.412 --> 00:07:16.245
- Always.

00:07:16.245 --> 00:07:17.078
- [Theresa] You're not
playing it on purpose.

00:07:17.078 --> 00:07:18.660
- No.
- Know that that is her soul,

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:21.900
her energy that is with
you at the exact moment.

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:25.740
So know that she wants
to thank you for that,

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:29.280
and know that everything
that you see is truly her,

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:30.900
and that she hasn't left you.

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:32.700
- Oh, thank you so much.

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:34.860
- Don't thank me, thank her.
- Thank (indistinct),

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:36.510
I love you you sissy.
- She's the one that did it.

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:38.610
- I love my sissy, she's the best.

00:07:38.610 --> 00:07:39.810
- Oh my God.
- Do we understand

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:41.400
the hitting of the head?

00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:42.931
- That was her, that's her.

00:07:42.931 --> 00:07:45.843
- Okay, and do you
think that she suffered?

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:48.870
- I think she did, it was
a tragic car accident.

00:07:48.870 --> 00:07:50.403
- 'Cause she hit me in
the back of the head.

00:07:50.403 --> 00:07:51.870
- Yes.
- And then what she did

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:53.760
is she then had this blow to the chest,

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:55.113
and she made me feel like,

00:07:56.670 --> 00:07:58.560
I immediately left the physical body.

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:00.870
- Okay, so I was told that before.

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:02.040
Oh my god, yes.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:03.187
- She says, "I need you to believe

00:08:03.187 --> 00:08:04.897
"that I did not suffer to my death,

00:08:04.897 --> 00:08:07.800
"or if anyone got to me sooner,
that I would still be here."

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:08.633
- Thank God.

00:08:08.633 --> 00:08:11.070
- Know that my soul immediately left.

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:12.600
- Oh, thank you God.

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:14.222
- I'm very sorry for the loss

00:08:14.222 --> 00:08:15.634
of your sister.
- Thank you so much,

00:08:15.634 --> 00:08:16.593
thank you so much.

00:08:16.593 --> 00:08:19.050
- I wish you all the best.
- I appreciate you.

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:19.883
- Thank you.
- God, you do this

00:08:19.883 --> 00:08:22.338
all the time, this is so intense.

00:08:22.338 --> 00:08:24.900
(audience applauding)
- I could keep going.

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:26.170
- This is so intense.

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:27.910
- [Theresa] Yeah.

00:08:29.370 --> 00:08:32.610
- That was overwhelming
to just be in the room

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:34.020
while all of that just went down,

00:08:34.020 --> 00:08:35.367
and you do that regularly, like?

00:08:35.367 --> 00:08:36.810
- And I could still go.

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:39.540
I mean, 'cause it's
almost like I felt like

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:41.880
when I first came out, people
like thinking, "Oh, my God."

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:42.713
And then it's almost like,

00:08:42.713 --> 00:08:44.610
"Oh, well I wonder if
my loved one is here."

00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:46.410
I think that was me, I should speak up,

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:47.880
I should say something.

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:50.250
So I just say to you all,

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:53.310
just embrace and know that the
things that go on around you

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:55.830
that remind you of your
loved one that has died,

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:57.510
to know that that is them,

00:08:57.510 --> 00:09:00.420
know that there is an afterlife.

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:01.590
And that they will greet us

00:09:01.590 --> 00:09:04.350
when we do leave this physical world.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:06.300
I can feel like there are so many people

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:08.280
that have a million questions,

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:10.260
a million questions right now.

00:09:10.260 --> 00:09:12.930
And I understand, and I read what respect.

00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:15.330
What I do is not for everyone,

00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:17.280
and I will never force messages on anyone.

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:18.450
- I can see how that might scare someone

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:19.500
to where they'd be quiet about it,

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:21.203
and then talk about it later.
- [Theresa] A 1000%, right.

00:09:21.203 --> 00:09:22.740
- Yeah, yeah.
And that's okay.

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:24.282
- It freaked me the hell out.

00:09:24.282 --> 00:09:25.710
(everyone laughing)

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:28.584
Well give it up Theresa Caputo everybody.

00:09:28.584 --> 00:09:29.490
(audience applauding)

